        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "111eea38-39de-53ee-83c5-547371dbb844",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Weinreich, Uriel Weinreich\n- Roles: linguists, sociolinguist, Yiddish scholar\n- Places: Kuldīga, Russian Empire, Latvia, New York City, United States\n- Concepts: Yiddish, sociolinguistics, “A language is a dialect with an army and navy”\n- Products: Modern Yiddish-English English-Yiddish Dictionary\n\nFacts:\n- Max Weinreich was born on 22 April 1894 in Kuldīga in the Russian Empire, now Latvia.\n- Max Weinreich was a Russian Jewish linguist who specialized in sociolinguistics and Yiddish.\n- Max Weinreich was the father of the linguist Uriel Weinreich.\n- Uriel Weinreich was born on 23 May 1926 and was a Polish-American linguist.\n- Uriel Weinreich edited the Modern Yiddish-English English-Yiddish Dictionary.\n- The adage “A language is a dialect with an army and navy” was popularized by the sociolinguist and Yiddish scholar Max Weinreich, who said he had heard it from an audience member at one of his lectures.\n- Max Weinreich died on 29 January 1969 in New York City, United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
